-- title:
--   Branch number at a node, unit form of ord = n
-- statement:
--   Let $q$ be a prime, $A$ a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, $k$ a field of characteristic $q$ and $red : A \to k$ a ring homomorphism; let $a \in k$ satisfy $a^{q^2} = a$, and let $K$ be a finite extension of $\mathbb{Q}$ inside $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$. Write $R_K =$ `coeffSubring A K` $= A \cap K$ and let $\varpi \in R_K$ be such that an element $c$ of $R_K$ has $\varpi \mid c$ exactly when the restriction `redRestrict red K` of $red$ to $R_K$ kills $c$. Let $g$ lie in `modularLocalizedAtPoint (1 * q) R_K (redRestrict red K) a (a ^ q)`, the subring of Laurent series $f$ over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ admitting $r, s \in R_K[X_0, X_1]$ with `pointEval` of $s$ at $(a, a^q)$ nonzero and $f \cdot \mathrm{ev}(s) = \mathrm{ev}(r)$, where $\mathrm{ev} =$ `modularEval (1 * q) R_K` sends $X_0 \mapsto$ `jqModC`, $X_1 \mapsto$ `jqNModC` of level $1 \cdot q$ and constants to constant series. Assume $g$, as a Laurent series, lies in `CharPReduction.modularLocalized (1 * q) A.toSubring red` (the localisation at the kernel prime of the subring generated by constants from $A$ together with `jqModC` and `jqNModC`), that its image $\bar g$ under `modularRedLocHom` lies in the field `modularFunctionFieldC k 1` generated over $k$ by `jqModC k` and `jqNModC k 1`, and that $\bar g \neq 0$. Then for $n \in \mathbb{N}$, the order $\mathrm{ord}$ of $\bar g$ at the place `(frobNodePair q a).1` $=$ `charLGeomPlaceOfPoint k a` equals $n$ if and only if there is a unit $u$ of `modularLocalizedAtPoint (1 * q) R_K (redRestrict red K) a (a ^ q)` with $g - \mathrm{ev}(X_0 - X_1^q)^n \, u$ in the ideal generated by $\mathrm{ev}(\varpi)$ and $\mathrm{ev}(X_1 - X_0^q)$.
--
--   This is the unit, or exact, form of the branch-number criterion at a node of the modular curve of level $q$ in characteristic $q$: the order of vanishing along the first branch of the reduction of $g$ is $n$ precisely when $g$ is congruent to $(X_0 - X_1^q)^n$ times a unit modulo the node ideal $(\varpi,\; X_1 - X_0^q)$. It is the shape used when extracting crossing presentations of local equations at the node and computing crossing exponents at level one.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_NodeLocalized_ord_modularRedLocHom_eq_iff_exists_isUnit.lean

